-- Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2, batch 5: the XML airframes and the mobile
-- bases. 9 rows (printed 169-192): the XML-280 Black Eagle, XML-283 Wraith
-- and XML-285 Ghost (vehicle_class borg: the Luftwaffe Cyborg Combat Pilot is
-- installed in them), the NGR standard deployment pod and XMF-1 drop fort,
-- the NGR Undertow, the TX-MISB mobile infantry strike base, its IA-30 APC,
-- and the AA-50.
-- See apps/character-creator/docs/surveys/triax-2.md.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
-- EVERY NUMBER WAS READ OFF A RENDER and checked against a render again by
-- book-reconcile; no figure disagreed. Every slug was queried against
-- production vehicles and gear before this file was written.
--
-- CONVENTIONS (as the Warlords of Russia vessels):
--   cost is the lowest printed price; the full wording is in cost_note. "Not
--     available" is NULL with the wording kept.
--   Locations and weapons are in printed order; a small target carries
--     "called shot only" in its mdc_note. Hand to hand tables and sensor
--     notes are in the description.
--   A book slip (a bad metric conversion, a location printed twice, a
--     missile mix that does not add up) is stored as printed and named in
--     the row.
--   The TX-MISB is one row; its forward, command and rear sections are
--     prefixed locations, and mdc_main_body is the command center's APC deck
--     (1,640), whose loss immobilises the base.
--   The Undertow's price is NULL: the book says it is not available and gives
--     only its 90 billion credit build cost, kept in cost_note.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-triax-2-airframes-and-bases.sql

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('xml-280-black-eagle', 'XML-280 Black Eagle', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One specially-modified Cyborg Combat Pilot.', NULL, NULL, 'Mach 2 (approximately 1,340 mph/2,144 km) maximum; engages at speeds as slow as 130 mph (208 km). Range effectively unlimited; maximum altitude 65,000 feet (19,812 m).', NULL, 'Height 13 feet (3.9 m) from belly to tip of tail fins; width/wingspan 34 feet (10.3 m); length 48 feet (14.6 m)', '19 tons fully loaded', 380, 1, NULL, 158000000, 'Black Market 158 million credits; NGR Luftwaffe only; not sold on the open market or the Black Market.', 'A small supersonic multi-role fighter and interceptor that exists only because of the Luftwaffe Cyborg Combat Pilot program: the pilot slides prone into the nose and is wired in within two melee rounds, so the jet is effectively his cybernetic body. It dives into Gargoyle flocks and roosts, dogfights winged Gargoyles and flying Brodkil, and strafes Gurgoyles and ground troops, usually fighting at 130 to 350 mph and flying through streets and canyons. Four wing hardpoints take XLH weapon pods. Called shots on asterisked locations are -4 (-10 at Mach 1 or more). Losing one wing halves speed, puts serious maneuvers at -50% even for the cyborg and forces a return to base; losing both crashes it. When the main body is gone the pilot may hold it together on an extra 10% M.D.C. (Elite Aerial Combat skill), and an automatic ejection and recovery system fires if it is destroyed in the air. Nuclear, 20-year life; no cargo; black or dark grey; carries the standard NGR aircraft sensors.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.169-170'),
('xml-283-wraith', 'XML-283 Wraith', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One specially-modified Cyborg Combat Pilot.', NULL, NULL, '560 mph (896 km) maximum; cruising 330 mph (528 km); can slow to a dead stop and hover, and fly sideways or upside down through narrow spaces. Range effectively unlimited; maximum altitude 45,000 feet (13,716 m), usually fights at 10 to 10,000 feet (3 to 3,048 m).', NULL, 'Height 6 feet (1.8 m) from belly to top of pilot compartment; width/wingspan 16 feet (4.9 m); length 22 feet (6.7 m)', '9 tons fully loaded', 300, 1, NULL, 125000000, 'Black Market 125 million credits; NGR Luftwaffe only; not sold on the open market or the Black Market.', 'A tiny arrowhead-shaped flying wing, smaller than most robots, with full thrust vectoring and a radar return easily mistaken for power armor; it can hug the ground under radar. The pilot lies prone in a housing at the rear and is wired in within two melee rounds. Wraiths strafe at 200-300 mph down the halls of skyscraper roosts and into Gargoyle aviaries, and punch holes for power armor and infantry. It has no hardpoints and never carries pods, relying on four lasers and six belly mini-missiles. Called shots on asterisked locations are -5 (-11 at 400 mph or more). Losing one wing costs 30% speed and -20% to piloting maneuvers; at two-thirds of the wing area gone speed halves and maneuvers are -50%; losing both crashes it. The pilot can hold a destroyed main body together on an extra 10% M.D.C., and it has automatic ejection. Nuclear, 20-year life; silver and royal blue.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.170-172'),
('xml-285-ghost', 'XML-285 Ghost', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One specially modified Cyborg Combat Pilot, plus up to three communications officers, depending on the mission.', NULL, NULL, 'Mach 3.5 (approximately 2,665 mph/4,264 km); VTOL capable through low profile hover jets in the undercarriage. Range effectively unlimited; maximum altitude 65,000 feet (19,812 m).', NULL, 'Height 13 feet (4 m); width 48 feet (14.6 m); length 64 feet (19.5 m)', '30 tons fully loaded', 440, 1, NULL, 190000000, 'Black Market 190 million credits; NGR Luftwaffe only; for now unavailable on both the open market and the Black Market.', 'The Luftwaffe''s newest fighter, an air-superiority stealth design with trapezoidal wings, built and hidden at a secret airfield in Poland. The cyborg pilot lies prone in his compartment and flies it alone; a second cockpit seats up to three officers for communications, sensors and electronic attack, and the Ghost coordinates troop movement and targeting for its air wing. Its chameleon skin changes color by thought (up to 15 seconds, 10 preset patterns) and leaves enemies -4 on Perception to spot it; radar detection is -75% and infrared -55%, missiles using infrared guidance strike at -3; with one bay open the radar penalty falls to -36%, and two or more open bays, external pods or active jamming make it visible. Sensors add AESA radar (600 miles, 64 targets, terrain following), secure links to 32 aircraft, jamming within 10 miles (Radio: Countermeasures and Sensory Equipment rolls at -40% to recover), LIDAR (200 miles), belly optics with a 6 mile zoom, a radar warning receiver (690 miles) and 1,000 mile encrypted radio and laser communications. Called shots on asterisked locations are -4 (-10 at Mach 1 or more); wing loss, last-gasp 10% M.D.C. and ejection follow the other XML airframes.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.172-174'),
('ngr-standard-deployment-pod', 'NGR Standard Deployment Pod', 'rifts', 'other', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'None under its own power; dropped from 30,000-50,000 feet (9,144 to 15,240 m), its hover jets slow the fall for a hard landing.', NULL, 'Height 10 feet (3.5 m); width 8 feet (2.4 m); length 14 feet (4.3 m)', '400 pounds (180 kg), empty', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'No price printed; availability Excellent.', 'A Triax ceramic M.D.C. cargo container about half the size of a boxcar ("drop pod" or "DP"), air-dropped from an XM-180 Dragonfly or XM-199 Phoenix to remote bases and operations and guided to a radio or laser marker; five hover jets under the floor and four small roof thrusters keep it upright and on target. It holds up to 38 tons, takes two transport slots, and anyone it lands on takes 1D4x10 M.D. A punched code drops one wall to unload, another frees the walls so troops can fold them away or use them as shelter or building material; only the jet floor panel should be sent back. Power is two rechargeable car-type batteries that can be reused or cannibalized. Standard loads include the Battle Gear Supply, Bunker (a 15 foot bunker, 80 M.D.C. per 15 square feet, ten soldiers in 12-16 hours), Force Field Generator (a 100 M.D.C. dome, 15 foot radius), Infantry Weapon, Power Armor (4-6 suits) and Sensor System pods. No Main Body line is printed.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.177-178'),
('xmf-1-drop-fort', 'XMF-1 Drop Fort', 'rifts', 'other', 'Troop support.', NULL, NULL, 'None; it cannot move of its own accord (air-dropped like a deployment pod with the same hover touch-down system).', NULL, 'Height 20 feet (6.1 m) to where the roof can rise, plus a 5 foot (1.5 m) roof cap for 25 feet (7.6 m) total; width/length 20 feet (6.1 m) in diameter', '8.8 tons', 1000, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Black Market: none; NGR only.', 'The Fortification Pod: a heavy modular M.D.C. strongpoint that is air-dropped like a deployment pod and lands to serve as a self-contained mini-command module. Its top rises so troops can fire from a reinforced position or be evacuated, standing on a ramp that winds around the top, and two mini-missile launchers drop from the ceiling when it is raised. Nuclear, 20-year life; no cargo; takes six transport slots. Its sensors are those common to NGR robots plus advanced radar (200 miles/320 km, 120 targets) and 500 mile (800 km) communications. Loses all function when the main body is reduced to zero.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.178-179'),
('ngr-undertow-submersible-carrier', 'NGR Undertow Submersible Carrier & Launching Base', 'rifts', 'vehicle', '6,000 total.', '35,000 troops (over six full army divisions), including the 12,480 soldiers of the Division of Elite Combat Troops.', 'Not possible.', 'Not possible.', 'Water surface 30 mph (48 km); underwater 40 mph (64 km).', 'Height 6,400 feet (1,951 m); width 4,800 feet (1,463 m); length 4,800 feet (1,463 m)', '1,140,000 tons fully loaded', 110000, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Market Cost: top secret, not available; building it with all standard features, weapons and troops cost 90 billion credits.', 'The NGRS-1001, the largest undersea vessel humans have built: a self-sufficient submersible city designed by Triax to carry the Operation Sea Storm forces undetected and stay at sea for months, with dormitories, a full hospital, VR and movie centers, gyms, sports areas, restaurants, pubs, gardens and a shopping area. Only one exists as of 109 P.A. Intake valves around the lower section drive water through turbines for thrust in any direction. Its embarked force includes mechanized infantry, power armor, an air battalion (among them 144 XML-280 Black Eagles and 576 XML-283 Wraiths), medical companies, Sea Mites, Sea Bats, up to six Poseidon submarines, X-6000 transformable subs, 5,000 sea sleds and lifeboats, plus 190,000 tons of extra cargo. Losing the bridge moves control to the secondary flight deck, or to the engine room at -20% piloting with weapons down until jury-rigged (1D6 hours); losing the lower section/loading dock leaves no docking, so troops launch only through the power armor and hangar hatches; losing the main body sinks it, and below 2.5 miles (4 km) it is crushed with all aboard. Sensors include 500 and 50 mile communications, sonar to 80 miles, radar to 100 miles, a 2 mile thermal imager and a telescopic system; its targeting computer gives all ship weapons +1 initiative and +1 strike, and 200 searchlights (1 M.D.C. each) ring it. Nuclear with hydro-electric backup, 12-year life.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.181-183'),
('tx-misb-mobile-infantry-strike-base', 'TX-MISB Mobile Infantry Strike Base', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Forward Section (TX-MISB-P1 Component A): 16 (two pilots, two co-pilots, three communications officers, three technical officers, six gunners). Command Center and Main Troop Carrier (Component B): 18 (eight gunners) plus a command staff of 96. Rear Section (Component C): 16. The two side APCs (Components D & E) carry their own crews.', 'Forward: 60 infantry in T-25 Uber body armor and 18 power armor troops. Command Center APC section: 120 infantry, 60 power armor troops, plus vehicles (4 X-1001 Ulti-Max II, 12 DV-39 Wolf drones, 1 DVO-1 aerial spy drone, 12 XML Wraith fighters, 3-6 giant robots under 25 feet). Rear: 60 infantry and 18 power armor troops, plus a hospital wing of 18 doctors, 3 Cyber-Docs, 24 nurses and 12 soldiers for 48 injured.', '40 mph (64 km) pulled by all five components; 23 mph (36.8 km) pulled only by the rear or forward sections. Separated: forward section 60 mph (96 km), Command Center 12 mph (19.2 km), rear section 12 mph (19.2 km).', NULL, NULL, 'Overall height 90 feet (27.4 m) at its highest point; width 112 feet (34 m) with both APCs attached; length 180 feet (54.8 m). Forward section 80 feet (24.4 m) high (70 feet/21.3 m to the main cannon), 60 feet (18.3 m) wide, 54 feet (16.4 m) long; Command Center 90 feet (27.4 m) high, 30 feet (9.1 m) wide, 90 feet (27.4 m) long; rear section 80 feet (24.4 m) high, 60 feet (18.3 m) wide, 56 feet (17 m) long.', 'Around 116,000 tons with all components (forward 34,000; Command Center 35,000; rear 23,000)', 1640, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Black Market: none; built under contract for the NGR military.', 'The final production model of the NGR "Misfit": a five-part rolling fortress (forward section, Command Center and Main Troop Carrier, rear section, and two detachable side APCs) that serves as a mobile command center wherever troops mass for a major offensive. Five are in the field as of 109 P.A.; one of the three Mindwerks-era prototypes survives. The forward section is a battering ram tipped with a 4,300 M.D.C. prow and the heaviest guns, led by a super-particle beam cannon; the central section carries the command deck, the main troop carrier and a force field over its lower deck; the rear section is a mobile hospital with a flak turret. Each component has its own nuclear plant (20-year life) and can drive alone. Called shots on asterisked locations are -3; losing both forward sensor arrays kills long-range sensors and radar, but other sections can relay. mdc_main_body stores the Command Center''s APC deck, the main body whose loss immobilizes the base; the other sections'' main bodies are locations. Troops can also ride the handholds of the forward section and fire from it (the book says 96 infantry and 16 power armor there, against 60 and 18 in the stat block). The Command Center tables list no locations for its particle beam and double-barreled turrets.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.183-189'),
('tx-misb-ia-30-infantry-apc', 'TX-MISB IA-30 Infantry APC', 'rifts', 'vehicle', '11: pilot, copilot, three communications officers, four gunners, and two reserve gunners.', 'One full company of 120 soldiers in body armor, or two platoons (60 troops) of power armor such as the X-11 Predator II, X-21 War Eagle, Hell Angel and Glitter Boys.', '70 mph (112 km) maximum when separated from the Command Center.', NULL, NULL, 'Height 30 feet (9.1 m); width 20 feet (6.1 m); length 70 feet (21.4 m)', '11,000 tons', 800, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Black Market: none; built under contract for the NGR military.', 'One of the two identical armored personnel carriers (TX-MISB-P1 Components D & E) that ride on either side of the Mobile Infantry Strike Base''s Command Center and break away to drop troops at other points or fight as separate units. Called shots on asterisked locations are -3. Its force field regenerates in six hours (33 M.D.C. per hour), and its weapons cannot fire while the field is up; losing the main body shuts the vehicle down. Carries the full Triax sensor suite. Either APC may be swapped for the AA-50 artillery carrier.', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.189-190'),
('aa-50-armored-artillery-troop-carrier', 'AA-50 Armored Artillery Troop Carrier', 'rifts', 'vehicle', '10: pilot, copilot, two communications officers, and six gunners.', '60 infantry soldiers in body armor and 12 power armor troops.', '50 mph (80 km) maximum when separated from the Command Center.', NULL, NULL, 'Height 30 feet (9.1 m) from bottom to tip of sensor antenna, 16 feet to the base of the main gun; width 20 feet (6.1 m); length 62 feet (18.9 m)', '15,000 tons', 1200, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Black Market: none; built under contract for the NGR military.', 'The "Alternative APC" (Alternative TX-MISB-P1 Components D & E), an artillery carrier that takes the place of an IA-30 Infantry APC on the Mobile Infantry Strike Base when heavy long-range support is expected, trading troop space for a particle beam main gun and short- and medium-range missile launchers. Built and deployed independent of the MISB as well. Called shots on asterisked locations are -3, and losing the main body shuts it down. Carries the full Triax sensor suite and a troop complement who can join the fight. Its table lists a Multi-Missile and Laser Turret (500 M.D.C.) that has no matching weapon entry, and the laser and ion turrets give their arc as "20%".', 'Rifts World Book 31: Triax 2 p.190-192');

